<title>VIETNAM: Vietnam says sells coffee worth $9 mln to Algeria.</title>
<headline>Vietnam says sells coffee worth $9 mln to Algeria.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam has agreed to sell coffee worth $9.0 million to Algeria in return for debt cancellation and will complete the shipment by the end of January, an official at the state coffee company, Vinacafe, said on Friday.</p>
<p>The official, who declined to be named, said three state companies recently provided coffee to the government at 70 percent of the government's pre-set price limit of $1,470 a tonne, or $1,029.</p>
<p>He gave no details of the amount of coffee that would be shipped to Algeria, though $9 million at $1,029 a tonne would make the volume 8,746 tonnes.</p>
</text>
